hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1456","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Thumailah told us, Husayn bin Waqid told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told us, on the authority of his father, He said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on the pulpit delivering a sermon, when Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein arrived, walking and stumbling, both wearing shirts. Two red ones. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down and carried them, then he said: “God has spoken the truth. Your wealth and your children are a trial. Indeed, I saw “These two boys were walking and stumbling, so I could not be patient until I got down and carried them.” Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Khuza’i commended him, Zaid told us. Ibn Al-Hubab, on the authority of Hussein, and he said: “I was not patient,” then he began his sermon."
